# Session rules are local-only — never committed (global rule).
CLAUDE.md

# Local secrets. Holds the suggestion endpoint (Discord webhook / Worker URL), which is baked
# into the built DLL. Committing it would put a live credential in git history forever.
src/Secrets.props

# Build output
src/bin/
src/obj/
bin/
obj/
dist/

# Working clones used by the Creator's Publish button. syncrepo/ is the live target — challenge
# data lives in TieriChallengesFFXIV-Sync, which is what the plugin fetches from. publicrepo/ is
# the pre-split leftover that publishing used to aim at; ChallengeExporter now refuses it.
syncrepo/
publicrepo/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# The repo root IS the dev-plugin folder, so build artifacts land here.
TieriChallengesFFXIV.dll
TieriChallengesFFXIV.pdb
TieriChallengesFFXIV.deps.json
*.zip

# Copied in by the CopyPanacheLibs target — owned by the PanacheUI repo, not this one.
PanacheUI.dll
SkiaSharp.dll
libSkiaSharp.dll

# Build output: cue audio copied next to the DLL. Source of truth is assets/sounds/.
# Anchored with a leading slash so it cannot also match assets/sounds/.
/sounds/

# Build output: background images copied next to the DLL. Source of truth is assets/backgrounds/.
/backgrounds/

# Build output: the help document copied next to the DLL by CopyHelpDocument, so HelpLibrary can
# read it at runtime. Source of truth is docs/HELP.md. Anchored so it cannot match that one.
# Missed when the help feature landed, which left a second HELP.md sitting untracked at the root
# of the PUBLIC repo — free to be committed by a wildcard add and to drift from the real one.
/HELP.md

# Build output: PanacheUI's icon PNGs copied next to the DLL by CopyPanacheIcons, so an installed
# copy can find them without a devPlugins folder (see Issues/005). Owned by the PanacheUI repo.
/Icons/

# Local-only credential notes. Never committed — see SECRETS.local.md itself for why.
SECRETS.local.md

# Local-only security design: Challenge Token anti-cheat thresholds, the identity/HMAC scheme,
# and the secrets inventory. Publishing exact detection thresholds is a roadmap for evading
# them, so the public design doc describes the shape and points here for the numbers.
SECURITY.local.md

# Ban ledger mirror written by the Creator's Bans tab: backup/bans-private.json plus dated
# history under backup/history/.
#
# THIS IS THE PLAINTEXT LEDGER — real character names and the reasons they were banned. It is
# the only readable record of who is banned (published hashes are one-way) and so the only way
# to lift one, which is exactly why it exists and exactly why it must never be published.
#
# This repo's origin is TieriChallengesFFXIV-PUBLIC. Anything committed here is world-readable
# the moment it is pushed, and git history is not something you can quietly take back.
# The ledger's home is the private vault repo; this folder is a staging copy, nothing more.
/banbackup/

# wrangler local state — account cache, build artefacts. Never useful in the repo.
worker/.wrangler/

# Python bytecode from the dataset sweep scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
